{% if launch.required_pdf %}
{{ "\n\n" -}}## Your document

`{{ launch.required_pdf }}`, under your artifacts directory above, is a document you write and compile yourself. Nothing else writes any part of it: not the title, not a section, not a figure, not a bibliography entry, and nothing recompiles it after you stop. Your submission is refused while that file is missing or is not a PDF.

Write the complete LaTeX source beside it -- `\documentclass` to `\end{document}` -- with your `.bib` and any figures you generate, then compile it from that directory with the `tectonic` already on your PATH:

```bash
cd {{ launch.artifact_dir }}/{{ launch.required_pdf.rsplit('/', 1)[0] }}
tectonic -X compile {{ launch.required_pdf.rsplit('/', 1)[1][:-4] }}.tex --keep-logs
```

Read what tectonic prints, fix your own source, and compile again until the PDF is there. The `research-paper-writing` skill ships a starter scaffold under `scaffold/` in its own directory; copy it into your artifacts directory and edit it freely, or write your own preamble instead.
{% endif %}
